==English==

===Etymology===
From {{L.}} {{term|attritionem||a rubbing against|lang=lat}}, from the verb {{term|attritus|lang=lat}}, past participle of {{term|atterere||to wear|lang=lat}}, from {{term|ad-||to, towards|lang=lat}} + {{term|terere||to rub|lang=lat}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|s|-}}

# wearing or grinding down by [[friction]]
# {{human resources}} A gradual, natural reduction in [[membership]] or [[personnel]], as through retirement, resignation, or [[death]]
# {{rfv-sense}} {{human resources}} A policy of [[decruitment]] by not recruiting following voluntary resignation or retirement.
# {{sciences}} The loss of [[participant]]s during an [[experiment]]

